IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa30-sch10-part1`

-- coa30-sch10-part2-a.l4: Schedule 10 (Recognised supervisory bodies), Part 2 (Requirements for recognition of a
-- supervisory body), paragraphs 5A to 8 (lines 20089-20173 of ukpga-2006-46.txt, coa30's ranges).
-- Generated by work/gen_part2a.py from the text; the quote lines are copied from the raw file by work/build.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ THIS PART. Part 2 states what a body "must have" for the Secretary of State to recognise it (para 2(2)(a))
-- and for recognition to survive (para 3(1)(a)). One relation is stated once: a requirement function says whether
-- the body meets the paragraph; where a paragraph also says what the required rule must say about a person, a second
-- function applies that content to the person (so the same relation is not written from both sides).
-- Open-textured words ("adequate", "satisfactory", "fair and reasonable", "effective") are the Secretary of State's
-- judgment and are plain BOOLEAN inputs: the fact that the body's rules or arrangements meet that description.
-- FALSE and NOTHING as in coa30-sch10-part1.l4: JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own words; NOTHING where it
-- does not decide.  Every "must have" function answers JUST FALSE when a limb is unmet (the bare-"must" forks in NOTES.md).

§ `Schedule 10 -- Recognised supervisory bodies`

§§ `Part 2 -- Requirements for recognition of a supervisory body (paragraphs 5A to 8)`

-- ---- paragraph 5A: Delegation etc. of tasks by competent authority; 5B: Consultation ----
-- src:20091 | 5A The body (“B”) must have rules providing that—
-- src:20092 | (a) in circumstances where and to the extent that a task delegated to B is reclaimed by the competent authority under regulation 3 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016, the competent authority may apply rules (and may vary the rules it applies) made by B in accordance with the requirements of this Part of this Schedule,
-- src:20093 | (b) in circumstances where and to the extent that a task delegated to B is reclaimed by the competent authority under regulation 3 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016 and is delegated to another recognised supervisory body, the other recognised supervisory body may apply rules (and may vary the rules it applies) made by B in accordance with the requirements of this Part of the Schedule, and
-- src:20094 | (c) in circumstances where and to the extent that a task is not delegated to B by the competent authority under regulation 3 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016, the competent authority may apply rules (and may vary the rules it applies) made by B in accordance with the requirements of paragraphs 12 to 16 of this Schedule.
@ref sch 10 para 5A Delegation etc. of tasks by competent authority (src:20091-20094)
GIVEN `the body has rules providing that where a delegated task is reclaimed by the competent authority the competent authority may apply and vary the rules made by B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has rules providing that where a reclaimed task is delegated to another recognised supervisory body the other body may apply and vary the rules made by B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has rules providing that where a task is not delegated to B the competent authority may apply and vary the rules made by B in accordance with paragraphs 12 to 16` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 5A the body meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the body has rules providing that where a delegated task is reclaimed by the competent authority the competent authority may apply and vary the rules made by B`
       AND `the body has rules providing that where a reclaimed task is delegated to another recognised supervisory body the other body may apply and vary the rules made by B`
       AND `the body has rules providing that where a task is not delegated to B the competent authority may apply and vary the rules made by B in accordance with paragraphs 12 to 16`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The body (“B”) must have rules providing that"

-- src:20096 | 5B The body must consult with the competent authority and with other recognised supervisory bodies in making or varying rules in accordance with the requirements of this Schedule.
@ref sch 10 para 5B Consultation (src:20096-20096)
GIVEN `the body consults the competent authority and other recognised supervisory bodies in making or varying rules in accordance with the requirements of this Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 5B the body meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the body consults the competent authority and other recognised supervisory bodies in making or varying rules in accordance with the requirements of this Schedule`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The body must consult with the competent authority and with other recognised supervisory bodies"

-- ---- paragraph 6: Holding of appropriate qualification ----

-- src:20098 | 6 (1) The body must have rules to the effect that a person is not eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor unless—
-- src:20099 | (a) in the case of an individual other than a third country auditor, he holds an appropriate qualification,
-- src:20100 | (aa) in the case of an individual who is a third country auditor—
-- src:20101 | (i) he holds an appropriate qualification,
-- src:20102 | (ii) he has been authorised on or before 5 April 2008 to practise the profession of company auditor pursuant to the European Communities (Recognition of Professional Qualifications) (First General System) Regulations 2005 ( S.I. 2005/18) and has fulfilled any requirements imposed pursuant to regulation 6 of those Regulations, or
-- src:20103 | (iii) he meets the requirements of sub-paragraph (1A).
-- src:20104 | (b) in the case of a firm ...—
-- src:20105 | (i) each individual responsible for statutory audit work on behalf of the firm is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor, and
-- src:20106 | (ii) the firm is controlled by qualified persons (see paragraph 7 below).
@ref sch 10 para 6(1) Holding of appropriate qualification (src:20098-20106)
GIVEN `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is a third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual holds an appropriate qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third country auditor was authorised on or before 5 April 2008 under the 2005 Regulations and has fulfilled the requirements imposed under regulation 6 of those Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third country auditor meets the requirements of sub-paragraph (1A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `each individual responsible for statutory audit work on behalf of the firm is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the firm is controlled by qualified persons` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 6(1) the person is not eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor under the rule the body must have` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the conditions of the rule are met`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor unless"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): sub-paragraph (1A) or paragraph 7 is not known
    WHERE
        `the conditions of the rule are met` MEANS
            IF `the person is an individual`
            THEN IF NOT `the individual is a third country auditor`
                 THEN JUST `the individual holds an appropriate qualification`
                 ELSE IF    `the individual holds an appropriate qualification`
                         OR `the third country auditor was authorised on or before 5 April 2008 under the 2005 Regulations and has fulfilled the requirements imposed under regulation 6 of those Regulations`
                      THEN JUST TRUE
                      ELSE `the third country auditor meets the requirements of sub-paragraph (1A)`
            ELSE IF NOT `each individual responsible for statutory audit work on behalf of the firm is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`
                 THEN JUST FALSE
                 ELSE `the firm is controlled by qualified persons`

-- src:20108 | (1A) The requirements of this sub-paragraph are that—
-- src:20109 | (a) the individual holds a professional qualification which covers all the subjects that are covered by a recognised professional qualification and that are subjects of which knowledge is essential for the pursuit of the profession of statutory auditor, ...
-- src:20110 | (b) the individual is an EEA auditor who—
-- src:20111 | (i) on or before IP completion day, holds a professional qualification which does not cover all those subjects,
-- src:20112 | (ii) on or before IP completion day, has been approved by the body or is in the process of seeking approval from the body, and
-- src:20113 | (iii) has met whichever of the requirements of sub-paragraph (1B) is specified in the body's rules , or
-- src:20114 | (c) the individual is a specified state auditor who—
-- src:20115 | (i) holds professional qualifications obtained in a specified state that are comparable to an appropriate qualification, and
-- src:20116 | (ii) has met a requirement to take an aptitude test or to complete an adaptation period, or to undertake both, imposed on the individual by the body in accordance with Part 2 of the Recognition of Professional Qualifications and Implementation of International Recognition Agreements (Amendment) Regulations 2023, if such a requirement is so imposed.
@ref sch 10 para 6(1A) The requirements of this sub-paragraph (src:20108-20116)
GIVEN `the individual holds a professional qualification which covers all the subjects that are covered by a recognised professional qualification and that are subjects of which knowledge is essential for the pursuit of the profession of statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is an EEA auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on or before IP completion day the individual holds a professional qualification which does not cover all those subjects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on or before IP completion day the individual has been approved by the body or is in the process of seeking approval from the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has met whichever of the requirements of sub-paragraph (1B) is specified in the rules of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is a specified state auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual holds professional qualifications obtained in a specified state that are comparable to an appropriate qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has imposed on the individual a requirement to take an aptitude test or complete an adaptation period or both in accordance with Part 2 of the 2023 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has met that requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 6(1A) the requirements of this sub-paragraph are met` MEANS
    IF    `the individual holds a professional qualification which covers all the subjects that are covered by a recognised professional qualification and that are subjects of which knowledge is essential for the pursuit of the profession of statutory auditor`
       OR (    `the individual is an EEA auditor`
           AND `on or before IP completion day the individual holds a professional qualification which does not cover all those subjects`
           AND `on or before IP completion day the individual has been approved by the body or is in the process of seeking approval from the body`
           AND `the individual has met whichever of the requirements of sub-paragraph (1B) is specified in the rules of the body`)
       OR (    `the individual is a specified state auditor`
           AND `the individual holds professional qualifications obtained in a specified state that are comparable to an appropriate qualification`
           AND (    (NOT `the body has imposed on the individual a requirement to take an aptitude test or complete an adaptation period or both in accordance with Part 2 of the 2023 Regulations`)
                 OR `the individual has met that requirement`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The requirements of this sub-paragraph are that"

DECLARE `sch 10 para 6(1B) requirement the rules specify` IS ONE OF
    `sch 10 para 6(1B)(a) a requirement to pass an aptitude test`
    `sch 10 para 6(1B)(b) a requirement to complete an adaptation period`
    `sch 10 para 6(1B)(c) a requirement either to pass an aptitude test or to complete an adaptation period at the choice of the individual`
    `sch 10 para 6(1B) another requirement`

-- src:20117 | (1B) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (1A)(b)(iii), the body's rules must specify one of the following requirements—
-- src:20118 | (a) a requirement to pass an aptitude test in accordance with sub-paragraph (2),
-- src:20119 | (b) a requirement to complete an adaptation period in accordance with sub-paragraphs (2B) and (2C), or
-- src:20120 | (c) a requirement either to pass an aptitude test in accordance with sub-paragraph (2) or to complete an adaptation period in accordance with sub-paragraphs (2B) and (2C), according to the choice of the individual.
@ref sch 10 para 6(1B) The requirements the rules of the body must specify (src:20117-20120)
GIVEN `the requirement the rules of the body specify` IS A `sch 10 para 6(1B) requirement the rules specify`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 6(1B) the rules of the body specify one of the requirements listed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the requirement the rules of the body specify`
    WHEN `sch 10 para 6(1B)(a) a requirement to pass an aptitude test` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 10 para 6(1B)(b) a requirement to complete an adaptation period` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 10 para 6(1B)(c) a requirement either to pass an aptitude test or to complete an adaptation period at the choice of the individual` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 10 para 6(1B) another requirement` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the body's rules must specify one of the following requirements"

-- src:20121 | (2) The aptitude test—
-- src:20122 | (a) must test the person's knowledge of subjects—
-- src:20123 | (i) that are covered by a recognised professional qualification,
-- src:20124 | (ii) that are not covered by the professional qualification already held by the person, and
-- src:20125 | (iii) the knowledge of which is essential for the pursuit of the profession of statutory auditor;
-- src:20126 | (b) may test the person's knowledge of rules of professional conduct;
-- src:20127 | (c) must not test the person's knowledge of any other matters.
@ref sch 10 para 6(2) The aptitude test: what it must, may and must not test (src:20121-20127)
GIVEN `the matter is a subject covered by a recognised professional qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is a subject not covered by the professional qualification already held by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `knowledge of the matter is essential for the pursuit of the profession of statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is a rule of professional conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 6(2) the aptitude test may test the person's knowledge of the matter` MEANS
    IF    (    `the matter is a subject covered by a recognised professional qualification`
           AND `the matter is a subject not covered by the professional qualification already held by the person`
           AND `knowledge of the matter is essential for the pursuit of the profession of statutory auditor`)
       OR `the matter is a rule of professional conduct`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not test the person's knowledge of any other matters"

@ref sch 10 para 6(2)(a) The aptitude test must test the subjects described (src:20122-20125)
GIVEN `the subject is covered by a recognised professional qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subject is not covered by the professional qualification already held by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `knowledge of the subject is essential for the pursuit of the profession of statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 6(2)(a) the aptitude test must test the person's knowledge of the subject` MEANS
    IF    `the subject is covered by a recognised professional qualification`
       AND `the subject is not covered by the professional qualification already held by the person`
       AND `knowledge of the subject is essential for the pursuit of the profession of statutory auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must test the person's knowledge of subjects" (the test may still test conduct under (b))

-- src:20129 | (2B) An adaptation period is a period, not exceeding three years, in which the individual (“the applicant”) pursues the profession of statutory auditor under the supervision of an individual who holds an appropriate qualification, subject to an assessment (“the ability assessment”) of the applicant’s ability to pursue the profession of statutory auditor in the United Kingdom.
@ref sch 10 para 6(2B) What an adaptation period is (src:20129-20129)
GIVEN `the length of the period in months` IS A NUMBER
      `the individual pursues the profession of statutory auditor under the supervision of an individual who holds an appropriate qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is subject to an assessment of the ability to pursue the profession of statutory auditor in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 6(2B) the period is an adaptation period` MEANS
    IF    `the length of the period in months` AT MOST 36
       AND `the individual pursues the profession of statutory auditor under the supervision of an individual who holds an appropriate qualification`
       AND `the individual is subject to an assessment of the ability to pursue the profession of statutory auditor in the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An adaptation period is a period, not exceeding three years"

-- src:20130 | (2C) Where the body’s rules specify a requirement that may or must be met by completing an adaptation period—
