-- ---- paragraph 7: what "controlled by qualified persons" means ----

-- src:20137 | (2) In this paragraph references to a person being qualified are—
-- src:20138 | (a) in relation to an individual, to that individual's—
-- src:20139 | (i) holding an appropriate qualification, or
-- src:20140 | (ii) being a third country auditor and meeting the requirements of paragraph 6(1)(aa)(ii) or 6(1A);
-- src:20141 | (b) in relation to a firm, to its—
-- src:20142 | (i) being eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor, ...
-- src:20143 | (ii) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref sch 10 para 7(2) References to a person being qualified (src:20137-20143)
GIVEN `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual holds an appropriate qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is a third country auditor and meets the requirements of paragraph 6(1)(aa)(ii) or 6(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the firm is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 7(2) the person is qualified` MEANS
    IF `the person is an individual`
    THEN IF    `the individual holds an appropriate qualification`
            OR `the individual is a third country auditor and meets the requirements of paragraph 6(1)(aa)(ii) or 6(1A)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references to a person being qualified are—"
    ELSE IF `the firm is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a firm, to its— being eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor"

-- src:20147 | (4) A majority of the members of a firm means—
-- src:20148 | (a) where under the firm's constitution matters are decided upon by the exercise of voting rights, members holding a majority of the rights to vote on all, or substantially all, matters;
-- src:20149 | (b) in any other case, members having such rights under the constitution of the firm as enable them to direct its overall policy or alter its constitution.
@ref sch 10 para 7(4) A majority of the members of a firm (src:20147-20149)
GIVEN `matters are decided under the constitution of the firm by the exercise of voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fraction of the rights to vote on all or substantially all matters held by the qualified members` IS A NUMBER
      `the qualified members have rights under the constitution that enable them to direct the overall policy of the firm or alter its constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 7(4) the qualified members are a majority of the members of the firm` MEANS
    IF `matters are decided under the constitution of the firm by the exercise of voting rights`
    THEN IF `the fraction of the rights to vote on all or substantially all matters held by the qualified members` GREATER THAN 0.5
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A majority of the members of a firm means— members holding a majority of the rights to vote on all, or substantially all, matters"
    ELSE IF `the qualified members have rights under the constitution that enable them to direct the overall policy of the firm or alter its constitution`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any other case, members having such rights under the constitution of the firm as enable them to direct its overall policy or alter its constitution"

